div.p:
§ 3. suscepta correctione morum: so Land some of the later MSS.;
the others have correptione, a word very often used by Christian writers.
For correctio morum (= censura) cf. Tib. 42, 1, in ipsa publicorum morum

p.note:
: Julia, daughter of Titus and Marcia Furnilla (Tit. 4, 2);
she was married to Flavius Sabinus, a cousin of Domitian, who was put to
death by the emperor (Dom. 10, 4).
